name: first blood
after: 08-cutting
intro: No hints from here on. No reference lookups, no tab, no manpage. Just the
intro: machine and what you already carry in your hands. Three questions on the
intro: one file every unix has. Build each pipeline a stage at a time and look
intro: at what each stage prints before you add the next -- that IS the skill.
---
setup: /etc/passwd is colon-separated. Field 1 is the username, field 7 the
setup: login shell. It is the first file you read on any machine you are handed.
q: count how many accounts exist
a: wc -l < /etc/passwd
a: cat /etc/passwd | wc -l
a: wc -l /etc/passwd
ref: wc
---
setup: You want just the names, nothing else around them.
q: print every username, one per line
a: cut -d: -f1 /etc/passwd
ref: cut
---
q: print every username, sorted alphabetically
a: cut -d: -f1 /etc/passwd | sort
ref: sort
